WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.702
-President Trump
has been scrambling

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:05.438
for literally any kind
of positive achievement

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.174
as he nears the end
of his first 100 days in office.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:11.644
Meanwhile, he and Congress are
facing down an imminent deadline

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.045
to avoid a government shutdown.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:15.848
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.585
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.155
Trump is nearing
the 100 day milestone

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.157
with record low approval ratings

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.958
and a White House
in constant chaos,

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.194
which means today
was the perfect day

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.997
for a jovial, well-rested
former President Obama

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.866
to show up in Chicago
for his first public appearance

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:35.868
after leaving office
and say this.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.638 line:0%
-So, uh...

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.807 line:0%
what -- what's been going on
while I've been gone?

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:41.874 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.911
[ Chuckles sarcastically ]

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.184
Everything!

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.653
Everything has been going on.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.355
Of course, after that comment,
Obama threw on some shades,

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:57.890
kite surfed
out of the auditorium

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.027
and yelled,
"Somebody get me a mai tai."

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:03.963
But Obama's first
post-election public appearance

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.398
was especially well-timed,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.168
because Saturday will mark the
100th day of Trump's presidency.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.202
Which is traditionally
when presidents get

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.805
their first big report card
on their performance so far.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.073
And this will shock you.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.809
Most people
think he's not doing great.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.345
-We have our brand-new NBC News
<i> Wall Street Journal</i> poll

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.313
so tell us
just how Americans think

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.549
the president is doing
as we approach Day 100.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.883
In short, not well.

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.420
-The worst approval ratings
around the 100 day mark

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.655
for any president
in modern times.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:32.825 line:0%
-He laid out a very detailed
100 day contract he called it --

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.595 line:0%
Obamacare, tax reform,
border wall funding,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.964 line:0%
infrastructure spending,
new trade tariffs,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.832 line:0%
labeling China
a currency manipulator,

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.834 line:0%
ending the common core
education standards.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.136 line:0%
100 days in or one week
from 100 days anyway,

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.605 line:0%
incomplete at best.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.941 line:0%
None of this,
none of this has been done.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.276
-None of this has been done.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.711
If this were a movie,
it would be called

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.914
"100 Dayz and Confused."

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.084
Now, the polls did have one bit
of good news for Trump,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.252
which if a new election
were held today,

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:02.989
Trump would win over Clinton
43% to 40%.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.290
And of course,

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.525
Trump could not help but brag
about those numbers,

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:07.594
tweeting yesterday...

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.203
Still?

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.139
Does he think he won
the popular vote the first time?

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.074
Because I got news for you,
buddy.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:24.877
You can't still do something
you've never done before.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.780
It's like me saying
"It's been 100 days,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.083
but Rihanna
would still go out with me.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.484
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.718
[ Applause ]

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.120
Thank you for sticking with me.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.359
Nonetheless, the 100 day
report card is on the way.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.960
And like every terrible student,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.462
Trump is trying to turn an "F"
into an "A,"

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.165
tweeting last week...

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:55.241
Yeah, the 100 day report card
is an arbitrary,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.444
meaningless political milestone
that most people care about.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.880
Most people, that is,
except Donald Trump.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.683
-I propose the contract
with the American voter.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:11.157
It's a set of promises for what
I'll do in my first 100 days.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.928
What follows
is my 100 day action plan

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.363
to make America great again.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.266
Just think about
what we can accomplish

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:24.503
in the first 100 days
of a Trump administration.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.605
-And then after
you thought about it,

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:30.075
tell me what you came up with,
because I've got nothing.

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:32.978
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:37.317
So as the 100 day milestone
nears,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.718
Trump has failed to deliver

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:41.387
on almost everyone of
his major legislative promises.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.989
Now, there are many reasons for
this including Trumps ignorance

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.092
about the basic political
realities of governing.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.527
In fact Trump is so ignorant,

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.362
he's ignorant
of his own ignorance.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.797
For example, he apparently
just learned

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.399
that there were
different factions

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.600
within the Republican Party

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.003
and talked about
as if it was a brilliant insight

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.805
telling the AP
in an interview...

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.915
Trump is like
an annoying 8-year-old kid

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.851
that just got home from school.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:15.287
Did you know fish can breathe
underwater by using their gills?

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:17.356
Yeah, Timmy, I did know that.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:21.694
Everybody knows that,
now go suck on your juice box.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.397
In fact, Trump even seems
to have trouble remembering

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:25.965
the names
of Congressional leaders

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.299
as we discover last week

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:31.136
when he kept referring to
House Speaker Paul Ryan as Ron

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:34.073
before catching himself
and trying to save it.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.442 line:0%
-My thanks goes to Speaker Ryan

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:41.113 line:0%
who's represented the city for
nearly two decades in Congress.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.815 line:0%
And you know where he is?

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.219 line:0%
He's with NATO, and --
So he has a good excuse.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.521 line:0%
I said, "Ron,
make sure these countries

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.323 line:0%
start paying their bills
a little bit more.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:54.093 line:0%
You know, they're way,
way behind, Ron.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.662 line:0%
I'm gonna talk to you
about that, Ron."

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.298 line:0%
But, Paul,
you're over with NATO,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.466 line:0%
get them to pay their bills.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.736
-I said Ron, "I mean,
I'm talking to you, Ron.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.504
Your names not Ron?
I meant Don.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:07.006
I was talking to myself.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.875
Don, you've got to get them
to pay their bills.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.511
Good idea, Don.
Thank you, Don."

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.146
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:18.084
So, with less than a week
to the 100 day deadline,

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.419
the Trump himself champion,

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.287
the president
has failed to deliver

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.922
on nearly every one of
his major legislative promises.

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:26.191
How could things get any worse?

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:27.926
-Shutdown showdown.

00:05:27.926 --> 00:05:29.195 line:0%
-The White House is racing

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.798 line:0%
to avoid marking the president's
first 100 days in office

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.165 line:0%
with a government shutdown.

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:35.534 line:0%
-If Congress doesn't send
President Trump

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.304 line:0%
a the government funding
bill midnight on Friday,

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.306 line:0%
the government
will run out of money

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.740 line:0%
and a shutdown would begin.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.909 line:0%
-A sticking point
as you may know

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:46.979 line:0%
is money for the wall
along our border with Mexico.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.214
-He could be the first President
in history

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:51.850
to face a government shut down
in his first 100 days.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.085
-Okay, but are we sure

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.321
the government
wasn't shutdown already?

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.790
Because it was reported recently
that...

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.531
Under Trump, our federal
government is staffed

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.935
as well as Duane Reade
on a Sunday morning.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.703
Hello?

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:15.541
Hello, I need my heart pills.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.177
Duane?

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.813
Reade?

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.349
So the White House is requesting
money for the border wall

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.683
and the bill
that funds the government.

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:27.653
But the crucial question is
will the president veto

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:30.689
any bill that does not include
money for the wall?

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:32.891
The government staying open
hangs on this question,

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:35.127
so when the AP asked Trump
that question point-blank,

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:39.699
this is what he said -- and this
is his full unedited answer.

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.998
As opposed to everything
up to that point,

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:14.734
which had been
super [bleep] telligible.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:16.468
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:20.839
So let's get back --

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:24.811
Let's get back
to his answer about the wall.

00:07:32.384 --> 00:07:33.486
I'll tell you one thing,

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.053
that answer would have
definitely made

00:07:35.053 --> 00:07:36.689
a much tougher chant
at Trump rallies.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.223
Who's going to pay for the wall?

00:07:38.223 --> 00:07:40.726
We don't know yet.
People want the border wall.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.761
Your base definitely
wants to border wall.

00:07:42.761 --> 00:07:45.263
You're base really wants it.
We've been to many rallies.

00:07:45.263 --> 00:07:46.933
Unintelligible.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.034
[ Applause ]

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:51.636
Now...

00:07:51.636 --> 00:07:54.039
Trump's answer on the wall
might be confusing for you

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:55.140
for many reasons,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.642
including the fact that,
as you may recall,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:08:00.813
Trump promised repeatedly that
Mexico will pay for the wall.

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:03.482
And on Sunday he took to Twitter
to settle the discrepancy

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:05.818
with his signature bravado
declaring unequivocally

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.286
that
without any hesitation that...

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.030
Trump's tweets are starting to
sound like the fine print

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.399
on a contest to win
a free cruise.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:21.234
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:35.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:39.418
Trump was also asked
how much the wall would cost?

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.888
And again
this is his real answer.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:53.532
Man, even the biggest sucker
at the used car lot

00:08:53.532 --> 00:08:56.902
knows to walk away when
the salesman says super-duper.

00:08:56.902 --> 00:08:58.070
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.705
And I'll tell you what,
I like you.

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.574
I'm gonna throw
the undercoating for free.

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:05.244
I just have to talk
to my manager, super-duper.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.446
Now publicly, Republicans
and the Trump administration

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.147
have downplayed the risk
of a government shutdown

00:09:09.147 --> 00:09:10.449
over border wall funding.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:12.118
But privately,
they seem excited.

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:14.887
One unnamed top White House
official told the<i> New Yorker...</i>

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:34.005
We've all been saying "get outta
here, it's too ridiculous"

00:09:34.005 --> 00:09:37.877
for two years,
yet here he is.

00:09:37.877 --> 00:09:40.012
Get out of here!

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:41.480
So, Trump...

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.584
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:48.187
So, Trump obviously has very few
concrete achievements

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:49.955
to celebrate
his first 100 days.

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:51.523
Which of course left Trump brag

00:09:51.523 --> 00:09:54.459
about the thing he loves to brag
about the most -- ratings.

00:09:54.459 --> 00:09:56.361
In fact Trump is so enamored
by ratings,

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:58.698
he's even basing major personnel
decisions on them.

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:00.498
<i> The Washington Post</i> reported
yesterday

00:10:00.498 --> 00:10:02.768
that when the prospect
of firing Sean Spicer came up

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.370
in a recent meeting,
Trump replied...

00:10:09.007 --> 00:10:12.210
Yeah, everyone tunes in
to watch Sean Spicer

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:15.681
for the same reason this video
has 31 million views.

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.950
[ Grunting ]

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.553
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.553 --> 00:10:25.458
Incidentally Trump just made
that guy Secretary of Pools.

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:28.293
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.293 --> 00:10:30.196
So Trump is facing a 100 day
milestone

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:32.231
with virtually no successes
to brag about,

00:10:32.231 --> 00:10:34.800
which may be why, when asked
by reporters last week

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.702
about
the sudden flurry of activity

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:38.637
and how his administration
was doing

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:40.105
as it neared
the 100 day deadline,

00:10:40.105 --> 00:10:43.509
he resorted to the most
meaningless platitudes possible.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.282 line:0%
-It's going to be great.
It'll happen.

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.750 line:0%
-You're gonna do healthcare
and tax reform?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.086 line:0%
-It'll happen.
We'll see what happens.

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:56.989 line:0%
No particular rush,
but we'll see with happens.

00:10:56.989 --> 00:11:00.125 line:0%
But healthcare is coming along
well.

00:11:00.125 --> 00:11:02.428 line:0%
Government is coming along
really well.

00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:05.397
[ Laughter ]

00:11:05.397 --> 00:11:07.332
-That's the President
of the United States saying

00:11:07.332 --> 00:11:10.335
government is coming along
really well.

00:11:10.335 --> 00:11:12.637
It's like going home to your
wife and saying,

00:11:12.637 --> 00:11:15.407
"Hello, wife, our marriage
is coming along really well."

00:11:15.407 --> 00:11:17.710
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.913
[ Cheers and applause ]

